diagnosis_text:
Affected component: LAN IP addressing/subnet mask on the PC12 access segment and the gateway’s matching interface; plus the EIGRP advertisement on r12. Mechanism: Both PC12 and its gateway r12.eth1 are configured with a /8 mask (255.0.0.0) for 120.1.1.x. This makes the entire 120.0.0.0/8 appear “on‑link” to both nodes. Traffic to any remote 120.x.x.x host gets ARP-resolved on the local wire, fails, and stalls for ARP timeout seconds before applications fall back to other IPs/paths—perceived as brief random “drops.” Localization: PC12 eth0 shows inet 120.1.1.10/8 and default via 120.1.1.1; r12 eth1 shows inet 120.1.1.1/8. From PC12, ip route get 120.2.2.2 returns “dev eth0 src 120.1.1.10,” and ping 120.2.2.2 fails (
